          "filename": "Timeball Skippy MRD 02.jpg",
          "caption": "A sculpture of Skippy, a Jack Russell cross who lived next door to the Lyttelton Timeball and visited the station every day at 1pm from 2003 until her death in 2009 to bark as the ball was lowered. The station was badly damaged in the February 22, 2011 Canterbury earthquake and as part of the restoration Waikari sculptor Sam Mahon created the statue.",
